# Assurance Matrix

This matrix is generated from the same catalogue as
`config/t40/control-manifest.yml`. Do not renumber rows by hand. Project teams
record decisions and evidence in the control manifest and the referenced
evidence documents.

`enabled` means installed but not yet evidenced. `verified` means every bound
check passed. `deferred` requires an owner and decision. `not_applicable`
requires the recorded manifest reason.

> This starter supports evidence gathering; it does not by itself provide ISO
> 27001, SOC 2, Cyber Essentials, WCAG conformance or legal compliance.

| ID | Control | Category | Status | Owner | Evidence checks | Production gate | Reference |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
<% controls.each do |control| -%>
| <%= control.fetch("id") %> | <%= control.fetch("name").gsub("|", "\\|") %> | <%= control.fetch("category") %> | <%= control.fetch("status") %> | <%= control["owner"] %> | <%= Array(control["evidence_checks"]).join(", ") %> | <%= control["production_gate"] ? "yes" : "no" %> | `<%= control.fetch("reference") %>` |
<% end -%>

The machine-readable control manifest is authoritative for current evidence and
readiness. Add project-specific controls to the catalogue rather than inserting
untracked rows here.
